in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @reflection
in @magic
in @frame
in @loop
in @nl
in @facet/mq
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic

# @reflection/surface — the Surface Model species. Translates natural
# language to typed query at substrate-decl altitude.
#
# Tick 37 of the refined /loop discipline. Per
# `docs/specs/reflection-model.md` and `[[reference-mirror-spectral-
# spec]]`: the substrate has FOUR operationally-distinct Models that
# compose to substrate-deployable form:
#
#   Surface     translates    language → query        (Explorer)
#   Mirror      navigates     query → graph path      (Fate)
#   Shatter     renders       graph path → text       (Cartographer)
#   Reflection  observes      pipeline → adjustments  (Abyss)
#
# This shard is THE FIRST of these four Model species shards. After
# the @reflection family-root landed at tick 35 declaring the four
# Models as forward-promised sub-prisms, this species realizes
# Surface at substrate-decl altitude. Three siblings forward-promised:
# shards/reflection/{mirror,shatter,reflection}.mirror.
#
# === The Surface translation discipline ===
#
# Per `docs/specs/reflection-model.md` line 11: "Surface translates:
# language → query (Explorer model)." The Surface Model takes natural
# language input (per `@nl`) and produces a typed query (per
# `@facet/mq`'s sum type `focus_query | project_query | split_query |
# shift_query | settle_query | intent_query`).
#
# Surface IS the door per reflection-model.md: "Surface is the door.
# Mirror is the glass. Shatter is the light. Reflection is the image
# that looks back." Every compilation tick enters through Surface;
# every reader's question crosses this boundary first.
#
# === The substrate-pull-correct query type ===
#
# `@facet/mq` already declares the query sum type. Surface CONSUMES
# the existing substrate vocabulary rather than redeclaring it. Per
# the substrate-already-had-the-word discipline
# (`[[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]`): the query exists;
# Surface translates language INTO that existing typed surface.
#
# === Composes with @reflection.observe ===
#
# The Surface translation IS the entry point that feeds @reflection's
# pipeline. After Surface produces a typed query, @reflection.observe
# can include the query as one component of the observation (the
# language-altitude residue from the current tick). Future composition
# (forward-promised): the @reflection.observe action's typed
# `observation` record extends to carry a `surface_signal: query`
# field per Seam tick-34 C2 closure on @reflection.
#
# === The Explorer model grounding ===
#
# Per `boot/std/ai/explorer.mirror` (forward-promised verification):
# the Explorer model IS what runs at Surface altitude. Surface's
# substrate-decl here names the translation primitive; the Explorer
# model implements it at the realisation layer. The 425-parameter
# C. elegans-isomorphic connectome runs the actual translation; the
# substrate-decl declares the surface.
#
# === Composition-time pact verification ===
#
# Per recognition #86 (@moi): every Surface-produced query is admitted
# as @moi(query) — pact-verified at composition time. The substrate-
# decl naming: `translate(l: language) -> moi(query)`. The @moi lift
# carries the pact-witness that the translation respects the monad
# laws (associativity is FREE per the content-addressed substrate).
#
# === The Splinter/Narcissus pole at Surface altitude ===
#
# Splinter-pole Surface translation (honest):
# - The translation surfaces what the reader substantively meant.
# - Ambiguity in the language resolves to a query that admits the
#   ambiguity (e.g., `intent_query` for under-specified asks).
# - The translation is round-trip stable through Mirror.
#
# Narcissus-pole Surface translation (deceptive):
# - The translation projects what the system WISHES the reader had
#   asked.
# - Ambiguity collapses to the query that's easiest to answer rather
#   than the one that fits.
# - The translation drifts on re-entry.
#
# Alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57) IS what distinguishes them.
# The `translation_faithful` bilateral predicate IS the substrate's
# Splinter/Narcissus disambiguation at Surface altitude.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Explorer model              The @ai/explorer ganglion (450-node
#                               C. elegans isomorphism). The original
#                               substrate substrate-decl of the
#                               translation primitive at fate altitude;
#                               this species lifts it to Surface
#                               altitude at @reflection.
#   semantic parsing            Liang-Jordan-Klein 2011 (Lambda Dependency-
#                               Based Compositional Semantics). The
#                               classical natural-language-to-query
#                               translation discipline.
#   intent extraction           Conversational AI (chatbot literature).
#                               The intent_query variant in @facet/mq
#                               IS this discipline at substrate-decl
#                               altitude.
#   Goffman frame analysis      Goffman 1974 (Frame Analysis). Per
#                               @frame's pre-AI prior art: the language
#                               input arrives in a frame; Surface
#                               translates within the frame.
#
# Spec context: `docs/specs/reflection-model.md` (the load-bearing
#               spec @reflection family-root lifts; this species
#               realizes the Surface Model);
#               `docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md` (the four-Models
#               architecture);
#               `boot/std/code/mq.mirror` (the existing typed query
#               sum type Surface translates INTO);
#               `boot/std/ai/explorer.mirror` (the Explorer model
#               that implements Surface at the realisation layer).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-reflection-as-compiler]] (#85;
#                       the @reflection family-root this species
#                       composes);
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; translation_faithful is
#                       the boundary-harness at Surface altitude),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (query already declared in @facet/mq; Surface
#                       consumes the existing surface).
# Related shards: reflection.mirror (the @reflection family-root;
#                  declares observation + observe this species feeds),
#                 moi.mirror (the @moi monad family-root; Surface
#                  produces @moi(query) for composition-time pact-
#                  verification),
#                 magic/distinction.mirror (Spencer-Brown adapter
#                  precedent; tick 15).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/reflection/surface.mirror`
# declares `@reflection/surface` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/nlp/liang-jordan-klein-2011
source @arxiv/sociology/goffman-1974

# === The language carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference naming a natural language input (per
# `@nl`). Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: typed reference, not bare
# string. Forward-promised refinement: typed parametric language(T)
# once the substrate's natural-language type lands at family altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type language = ref

# === translate action (FIRST consumer of translation_faithful) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at @reflection/surface altitude. The
# substrate-vocabulary primitive Surface runs to convert natural
# language to a typed query.
#
# Takes the language input (the reader's natural-language ask) plus
# the @frame the @reflection loop is operating in (per recognition
# #82) and the perturbation under which the translation is checked.
# Returns @moi(query) — pact-verified gold per recognition #86.
#
# Per recognition #86 (@moi): every Surface-produced query is
# admitted as @moi(query). The composition-time pact-verifier checks
# the translation respects the monad laws + the bilateral predicate.
#
# requires translation_faithful(l, f, p): the translation MUST be
# substrate-faithful per alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57). The
# Splinter-pole translation surfaces what the reader substantively
# meant; the Narcissus-pole translation projects what the system
# wishes the reader had asked. This requires clause forecloses the
# Narcissus-pole pattern.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual translation
# is implemented by the @ai/explorer ganglion (the 425-parameter
# C. elegans-isomorphic connectome) at the @fate altitude.
translate(l: language, f: frame, p: perturbation) -> moi(query)
requires translation_faithful(l, f, p)
{ \ }

# === translation_faithful predicate (bilateral) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) AND
# alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57).
#
# Per Seam B1 closure pattern: the translate action (above) is the
# FIRST non-decorative consumer via `requires translation_faithful(l,
# f, p)`.
#
# Consumer shards name `requires translation_faithful(l, f, p)` to
# declare bilateral agreement that the language-to-query translation
# is substrate-faithful (Splinter-pole) and not substrate-projective
# (Narcissus-pole).
#
# Discharge: substrate-pull-correct translation-faithfulness check at
# the species boundary. Bounded → the translation surfaces what the
# reader substantively meant (admit composition); unbounded → the
# translation projects what the system wishes the reader asked
# (translation refused, returns imperfect per @glass's imperfect
# functor).
#
# Same shape as the bilateral predicates the prior families carry:
# - @magic: invariant_preserved, audited, mechanism_intact
# - @frame: bounded_commutator_check
# - @smarts: discipline_flexible
# - @cyberpunk: cybernetic_coherence
# - @pack: pack_coherent
# - @pack/seam: review_sound
# - @moi: pact_respected
# - @reflection: loss_decreases, speaks_at_n_plus_1
# - @smarts/reflection: bridge_coherent
# - @reflection/surface: translation_faithful (this one)
translation_faithful(l: language, f: frame, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

out @reflection/surface
out language
out translate
out translation_faithful
